# MT5 / DWX bridge directory — the default for MT5_BRIDGE_PATH.
#
# This directory is bind-mounted into the backend at /app/mt5-bridge. It exists
# in git because Docker creates a missing bind-mount source as a ROOT-OWNED
# directory, and the backend container runs as uid 1001 and must WRITE here —
# it writes DWX_Commands_0.txt to subscribe to symbols. Without this the mount
# succeeded and symbol subscription failed with EACCES.
#
# deploy.sh chowns it to 1001:1001. If you set MT5_BRIDGE_PATH somewhere else,
# that directory needs the same ownership.
#
# Files a real MetaTrader 5 terminal (with the DWX expert advisor attached)
# writes here:
#   DWX_Market_Data.txt      — the tick stream the price feed reads
#   DWX_Commands_0.txt       — written BY the backend, to subscribe to symbols
#   DWX_History_Export.json  — candle history for the charts
#
# The terminal runs OUTSIDE these containers: the backend image is
# node:20-alpine and contains no MetaTrader. See DEPLOYMENT_CHECKLIST.md.
